<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 1.00 pct from parity rates.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 1.00 pct from parity rates.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2640 to the dollar, down from 3.2590 on Thursday, and at 1.8850 to the mark, up from 1.8870, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.00 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, slightly weaker than Thursday's 1.02 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
